        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.639,
            0.049,
            0.846,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": "Constructions and Tilings"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.088,
            0.435,
            0.109
          ],
          "content": "**Construction of a** $6 0 ^ { \\circ }$ **angle**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.111,
            0.484,
            0.135
          ],
          "content": "How do we construct a $6 0 ^ { \\circ }$ angle?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.138,
            0.846,
            0.176
          ],
          "content": "We get a $6 0 ^ { \\circ }$ angle if we construct an equilateral triangle! We can use the following steps for this."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.176,
            0.747,
            0.197
          ],
          "content": "Suppose we need a $6 0 ^ { \\circ }$ angle at point A on a line segment AX."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.2,
            0.222,
            0.221
          ],
          "content": "**Step 1**"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.372,
            0.24,
            0.615,
            0.31
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_17_image_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.319,
            0.721,
            0.339
          ],
          "content": "Construct an arc with centre A and any radius."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.359,
            0.222,
            0.381
          ],
          "content": "**Step 2**"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.402,
            0.38,
            0.508,
            0.491
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_17_image_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.514,
            0.792,
            0.554
          ],
          "content": "With the same radius, cut another arc from B that meets the first arc. Let C be the point at which the arcs meet."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.576,
            0.369,
            0.597
          ],
          "content": "We have $\\angle CAX = 60^{\\circ}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.611,
            0.709,
            0.659
          ],
          "content": "Why is $\\angle CAX = 60^{\\circ}?$ Is there an equilateral triangle here? We can use these ideas to construct a regular hexagon —"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.383,
            0.675,
            0.638,
            0.804
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_17_image_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.853,
            0.618,
            0.878
          ],
          "content": "Construct a regular hexagon of sidelength 5 cm."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.807,
